        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1bf39397-82c8-5824-a679-973922508b0a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fabian Cowdrey, Chris Cowdrey, Colin Cowdrey\n- Organizations: Kent County Cricket Club, England cricket team\n- Topics: cricket records, family lineage in cricket\n\nFacts:\n- Colin Cowdrey made 22 Test centuries for England, and that total remained an England record until 2013.\n- Colin Cowdrey was the first batsman to score centuries against the six other Test-playing countries of his era: Australia, South Africa, the West Indies, New Zealand, India, and Pakistan.\n- Colin Cowdrey made centuries against each of those six countries both at home and away.\n- Fabian Cowdrey became the first third-generation player to play for Kent County Cricket Club.\n- Fabian Cowdrey followed his father Chris Cowdrey and his grandfather Colin Cowdrey as Kent players.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a5905dc8-265c-5257-b6f3-9d3eef19775c",
        "text": "Page: Fabian Cowdrey. Sentence: He made history by becoming the first third generation player to play for the county, following his father, Chris Cowdrey, and grandfather Colin Cowdrey.\nPage: Colin Cowdrey. Sentence: Cowdrey made 22 Test centuries (an England record until 2013) and was the first batsman to make centuries against the six other Test playing countries of his era; Australia, South Africa, the West Indies, New Zealand, India and Pakistan, making hundreds against them all both home and away.",
